summary:
Iter49 — Tested Super-Admin App Logo feature (backend + frontend). Backend pytest 15/15 PASS. Verified: (1) PUT /api/admin/logo with PNG data-URL as super_admin → 200 {success:true, has_logo:true}, GET /api/appearance reflects has_logo:true + logo_url:/api/appearance/logo + non-zero logo_version, GET /api/appearance/logo returns 200 image/png. (2) Validation: invalid base64 → 400, image/gif data-URL → 400, oversized (>1MB raw) PNG → 400 with '1 MB' message. (3) AuthZ: PUT + DELETE as admin@test.com (non-super) → 403; unauth PUT → 401. (4) DELETE as super_admin → {has_logo:false}; subsequent /appearance/logo → 404 and /appearance has_logo:false. (5) PDF + Logo: with logo SET, /api/reports/dezider/<id>.pdf returns 200 application/pdf with %PDF magic, and with logo REMOVED, PDF still returns 200 — both paths verified for the existing dezider decision 9420c8cc... (used admin payment-settings skip_payment_all_flows=ON to bypass L1 gate during the test then restored to false). (6) Regression: /api/appearance still returns font_family='Inter', font_options[] (8 entries), company_name='HOORECON IT-Sys Pvt Ltd'. Frontend (desktop 1280x900): /admin/appearance renders correctly with NEW 'App Logo' section showing PNG/JPG/1MB hint, preview placeholder (image-outline icon), and 'Upload logo' purple button — alongside existing Company / Legal Name editor + Save button and 8-font picker with Inter pre-selected. Marketing landing (/) shows 'JELCOS AI' brand + tagline 'Joyful Executive's Life Choices Operating System — Powered by AI' in the header. Footer contains 'HOORECON' company name. Login screen (/auth/login) renders with the default JELCOS logo fallback (no admin logo set), JELCOS AI heading, tagline, Email/Password inputs, Sign In button, Google OAuth, Sign Up link. Zero console errors on the marketing page. CRITICAL FIX APPLIED: /app/frontend/app/auth/login.tsx had a 3-line dangling fragment after the StyleSheet close ('});
: COLORS.textMuted,
  },
});') at lines 683-685 which caused 'SyntaxError: Unexpected token (683:0)' and bricked the entire web bundle (Metro returned 500 for every script). After removing the malformed trailing fragment, bundle compiles cleanly (Web Bundled 2677ms, 1369 modules) and all screens load. LOGO LEFT REMOVED per the agent-to-agent-context note: GET /api/appearance/logo → 404, has_logo:false at end. No expo/react-native deprecated packages detected; no red-screen errors.
